WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.080
Halloween. Samhain. All Hallow's Eve. Whatever&nbsp;
you call it, it's known as the time of year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:12.120
when the veil between the land of the living&nbsp;
and the spirit world is at its thinnest. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.340
the time of things going bump in the night,&nbsp;
carving pumpkins, slipping on a rubber mask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.620
and getting ready to terrorize the neighborhood.&nbsp;
Whether you celebrate by going door to door and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.240
extorting strangers for candy, staying in&nbsp;
and watching scary movies in your pajamas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.680
or going out to wreak a little havoc&nbsp;
with eggs and rolls of toilet paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.840
just about everyone likes to mark the&nbsp;
day with a little bit of spooky fun. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:42.780
The folks at the SCP Foundation are no exception!&nbsp;
Sure, they see plenty of horrors in their everyday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.120
lives, but that doesn't mean they've lost the&nbsp;
holiday spirit! Around Halloween, staff can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.920
find Jack-O-Lantern shaped sugar cookies waiting&nbsp;
for them in the break room alongside hot cider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.540
and there is a yearly party in the canteen&nbsp;
with Halloween tunes, bobbing for apples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:03.000
and even a costume contest! But for some,&nbsp;
these festivities don't quite cut it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.400
They're not creepy, spooky, or ooky enough&nbsp;
to truly celebrate the scariest holiday. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:15.960
By "some," I, of course, mean Dr. Jack Bright,&nbsp;
everyone's favorite immortal human consciousness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:21.600
living inside an anomalous necklace.
 
Dr. Bright was determined to take last Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.120
up a notch, and he gathered his supervisors&nbsp;
together to pitch his latest brilliant idea:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.000
a haunted house, open for one night only,&nbsp;
filled with frightening anomalies from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.560
SCP Foundation. His request for resources&nbsp;
and permission to put the haunted house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.960
together were swiftly denied, but Dr.&nbsp;
Bright is nothing if not determined. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.220
Without the use of official funds, he&nbsp;
began plotting. He tracked down a venue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.840
a large abandoned farmhouse a few miles away&nbsp;
from the Site, he found a discount Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.360
supply store, and he watched hours of crafting&nbsp;
tutorials on YouTube to put together the best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.520
the scariest, the most memorable house&nbsp;
of horrors anyone had ever seen.
 &nbsp;

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.780
He planned the launch of his haunted house&nbsp;
attraction to coincide perfectly with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.220
annual office party. While his colleagues were&nbsp;
busy dancing the Monster Mash and enjoying the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:16.560
apple cider, Dr. Bright was getting ready to&nbsp;
open the doors, unveil his months of hard work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:22.740
and scare the pants off of any customers who dared&nbsp;
step inside. However, in all his preparations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.660
he had forgotten to spread the word to&nbsp;
the nearby community, except for an ad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:33.660
he purchased on Instagram. So, when Dr. Bright's&nbsp;
House of SCP Horrors opened for business, only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:39.240
three people were waiting to purchase a ticket:&nbsp;
Janie, Maddie, and Zach, a group of high school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.620
sophomores looking for something to do before the&nbsp;
Halloween party in the woods later that night. 
 &nbsp;

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:49.200
As the doors creaked open, Dr. Bright ushered&nbsp;
the teens inside with a wave of his hand. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.580
dressed up as Dracula, complete with a cape&nbsp;
and a pair of plastic fangs. When he spoke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:59.940
he affected a comical vampire accent: "Velcome,&nbsp;
children! Prepare for nightmares that vill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.680
last a lifetime!" He waited for his guests&nbsp;
to acknowledge his incredible performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:10.200
but they just stared at him blankly for a moment.
 
"Um...are you done?" Janie asked. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.160
Dr. Bright cleared his throat, suddenly&nbsp;
self-conscious. "Admission is five dollars." 
 &nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.380
The three teens shrugged,&nbsp;
and handed over the money. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:21.420
"Enjoy! Oooooooooo!" He backed out&nbsp;
of the room with a ghostly wail.  
 &nbsp;

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:28.420
"Ok...byeeee..." Maddie called after him. 
 
"Follow me into the first room! Ooooooo!"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:35.220
Dr. Bright's voice came from around the corner. 
 
"I guess we just...go that way?" Zach followed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.840
voice, and his friends joined him, as they walked&nbsp;
into a makeshift laboratory where Dr. Bright was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.300
waiting. The lights were dim; a steel table sat&nbsp;
in the corner covered in something dark, red,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:50.520
and wet. In the darkness, a cloaked figure&nbsp;
moved about, his face a long, beaked mask,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:55.620
his hands covered in thick black gloves. 
 
"Welcome, new patients, to the lab of The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:01.320
Plague Doctor!" Dr. Bright declared. Behind&nbsp;
him, SCP-049 was performing an experiment on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:06.180
the remains of a cow. With the flip of a switch&nbsp;
on the wall, a flash of electricity crackled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.660
illuminating the room as the Plague&nbsp;
Doctor looked up to greet the newcomers.&nbsp;

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.660
"Oh, welcome! May I show&nbsp;
you what I've been working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:17.760
on?" He held up a long, gleaming scalpel. 
 
"Is that it?" Maddie remarked, unimpressed.
 &nbsp;

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.860
"I think that's it," Zach replied. 
 
"Kind of boring," Janie sighed.
 &nbsp;

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.400
If he could, the Plague Doctor would&nbsp;
have frowned. "I am but a humble man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.600
of science, doing my work. If that is not&nbsp;
sufficient for you, then I apologize..."
 &nbsp;

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:36.120
"It's fine, Doc, don't worry." Dr. Bright opened&nbsp;
the next door. "Follow me, and have your spines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.760
tingled by the next terrifying chamber!" 
 
"Ew." The group of teens laughed. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.940
they had already spent five dollars on&nbsp;
this thing. Might as well see it through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.620
and tell everyone at the party later about&nbsp;
this weird man and his awful haunted house. 
 &nbsp;

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:54.060
Dr. Bright led the group down a long,&nbsp;
narrow hallway. It smelled of rotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.840
wood and mildew, the carpet squishing&nbsp;
unpleasantly beneath their feet. 
 &nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.400
"Keep an eye on your surroundings..."&nbsp;
Dr. Bright called over his shoulder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.420
"We might not be alone in here..." 
 
Behind him, the kids rolled their eyes. 
 &nbsp;

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:10.440
"Just don't touch the walls,"&nbsp;
Dr. Bright said, ominously. 
 &nbsp;

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.000
The group followed him, not the least&nbsp;
bit nervous. It was a creepy old house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.440
but there was nothing in here scarier than&nbsp;
a cockroach. As Janie felt something crunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.940
beneath her shoe, she stopped to take a look. 
 
"Ugh..." She groaned. When she looked up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.620
she noticed something strange. Black goo,&nbsp;
dripping down the wall next to her. "God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:32.940
this place is gross." She grimaced. Her&nbsp;
friends turned to see what made her fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:37.020
behind, and their eyes widened. 
 
"Janie..." Maddie's voice wavered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.600
slightly. Zach pointed. 
 
"Behind you..." 
 &nbsp;

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:45.180
Janie spun around, and was confronted with&nbsp;
a horrific figure. SCP-106 was emerging from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:50.580
the desiccating wall, smiling at her with a&nbsp;
wide, toothless grin, his flat eyes filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:55.440
with malice. She gasped, but then stopped. 
 
"Oh, it's just an old guy. It's fine." 
 &nbsp;

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.980
"Nice try, grandpa!" Zach laughed.
 
"Follow me, please! Move away from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:03.360
wall! Please!" Dr. Bright was beginning&nbsp;
to regret bringing SCP-106 into his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.920
attraction. It seemed a bit too dangerous,&nbsp;
now that he thought about it. "Quickly!"  
 &nbsp;

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.940
"Okay, what's next?" Maddie linked&nbsp;
arms with her friends, pulling them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.800
after their incredibly cringe tour guide. 
 
"Well, you're about to find out! If you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.280
handle it..." Dr. Bright opened a&nbsp;
door with a big sweeping gesture.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:26.220
"Step inside...the kitchen. Of DEATH!"
 
"Ooh, what's for dinner?" Janie quipped. 
 &nbsp;

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:30.480
"Doom." Dr. Bright grinned. 
 
The visitors and their guide walked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:35.820
into a dingy kitchen, rusty pots hanging from the&nbsp;
ceiling, a wood stove crackling in the corner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:40.740
something fuzzy, green, and unidentifiable&nbsp;
growing in the sink. The first thing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:45.240
greeted the group, aside from the smell of meat&nbsp;
sizzling in a pan, was the sound of a bellowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:50.160
male voice singing an operatic aria. Sure&nbsp;
enough, there at the stove, wearing a chef's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:55.920
hat that appeared comically tiny on his massive&nbsp;
head, was a giant of a man, singing. He wore a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:01.800
blood-stained apron reading "kiss the cook." 
 
"Oh, welcome! Who's hungry? I've been cooking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.820
all evening! It's an old recipe I learned&nbsp;
while studying under Julia Child at her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:12.420
culinary academy, a truly famous dish. I'm her&nbsp;
nephew, you know! Fernand Child! I keep her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:17.520
memory alive by preparing my favorite meals of&nbsp;
hers. Though I didn't use chicken for this one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.860
I selected a different protein..." The giant&nbsp;
man held out a serving spoon, shoving it into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.820
Zach's face. "Want a taste?" 
 
Zach recoiled. "No thanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.700
man, I'm a vegetarian." 
 
"Suit yourself, more for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:34.740
rest of us! Any takers?" Fernand offered the&nbsp;
spoon to Maddie, who shook her head. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.860
to Janie, who seemed to consider it for&nbsp;
a moment, but then turned it down. 
 &nbsp;

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:42.420
"Fernand is what I like to call a&nbsp;
'humanitarian'," Dr. Bright quipped. 
 &nbsp;

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:47.820
"Thank you sir, I do enjoy my charity work!"&nbsp;
Fernand saluted him. "Oh, and we do have another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:51.420
guest joining us for dinner, correct?"
 
"That's right! Though she prefers her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:56.400
meat rare. So rare, in fact..." Dr. Bright&nbsp;
grinned wickedly. "That it's still alive." 
 &nbsp;

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.480
"I've set a place for her already!"&nbsp;
Fernand gestured to a small table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:05.220
where a plate held a large serving of raw&nbsp;
liver. Next to it, an open bottle of wine. 
 &nbsp;

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:10.080
Behind the little group, a woman swept through&nbsp;
the door. She was beautiful, but eerie somehow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:15.420
Her eyes glinted with a feral cleverness, and&nbsp;
under her thick dark hair were a pair of fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:20.400
ears. A tail swished behind her as she walked,&nbsp;
and her fingernails were more like jagged claws. 
 &nbsp;

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:26.340
"Did you start without me? How rude." Her voice&nbsp;
had an edge to it, the same vaguely menacing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:31.320
inhuman quality that hung over the rest of her. 
 
"She's pretty hot..." Zach whispered. 
 &nbsp;

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:36.300
"Shut up!" Maddie elbowed him. 
 
"No, he's right, she is," Janie piped up.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:40.500
The woman barely acknowledged them, instead&nbsp;
walking to her place at the table. She picked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.820
up the liver in her hands, and opened her&nbsp;
mouth to reveal unnaturally sharp teeth. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:49.680
she dug in with the ravenous hunger of a caged&nbsp;
animal that had not been fed in far too long.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.380
"Terrifying, isn't she?" Dr. Bright urged.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.600
"Not really," Maddie shook her head.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.600
"What else you got?" Zach&nbsp;
raised an eyebrow. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.120
the fox woman had finished her&nbsp;
meal and moved on to the wine.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.100
"Can I get some of that?" Janie asked.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:08.400
"No! No underage drinking in my haunted&nbsp;
house! Only! Scares!" Dr. Bright sputtered.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.140
"Fine, whatever, just follow me."

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:14.520
He led the group onward, leaving Fernand and&nbsp;
the Polymorphic Humanoid to their strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.780
cannibalistic dinner party.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:20.760
"If you aren't in the mood for a meal, perhaps&nbsp;
you'd like to watch a little...television?" Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:25.140
Bright gave a villainous cackle as he threw&nbsp;
open the door to the living room. It was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:31.620
least eerie room so far, a standard living room,&nbsp;
if a bit dusty. There was an overstuffed chair, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:37.080
couch, a coffee table, a lamp in the corner, and a&nbsp;
vintage tv set plopped down in front of the couch.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:41.340
"How do you all feel about&nbsp;
clowns?" Dr. Bright asked.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:45.720
"Oh no, no, no, I hate clowns."&nbsp;
Janie's face went pale.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.300
"It's gonna be fine." Maddie patted her shoulder.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:51.060
"Not like it'll actually be scary," Zach scoffed.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.800
"Don't be so sure. Check THIS out!"&nbsp;
Dr. Bright switched on the tv,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:01.800
which began playing an episode of SCP-993,&nbsp;
Bobble the Clown. Unfortunately for Dr. Bright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:07.200
but fortunately for Janie, he had forgotten&nbsp;
that SCP-993 doesn't show its more upsetting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.480
content to anyone over the age of ten. The three&nbsp;
teenagers immediately collapsed, unconscious. 
 &nbsp;

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:17.580
"Oh dammit, oh no-" Dr. Bright scrambled to&nbsp;
switch the tv back off. As soon as the screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:22.380
went black, the kids sat up, disoriented&nbsp;
and rubbing their heads. "Sorry about that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:27.780
technical difficulties. I mean- Ooooooooo,&nbsp;
scary scary technical difficulties!" 
 &nbsp;

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:32.160
The kids stared at him blankly.&nbsp;
"Um. Claudia, a little help here?" 
 &nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.880
The three friends looked around, expecting&nbsp;
to see someone else in the room with them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:39.600
but there was no one.
 
"Are you feeling ok?" Maddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.420
looked genuinely concerned. 
 
"He's fine!" A voice piped up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:45.180
just behind her. "Are you?" 
 
Maddie spun around, looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:49.320
for the source of the voice, but there was no&nbsp;
one there. "Oh, I get it, you've got a hidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:52.260
speaker in here or something, right?" 
 
"Nope!" The mysterious voice laughed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:56.520
"It's just me. Hey, watch this!" 
 
Suddenly, Janie's phone floated out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.820
of her pocket, hanging in the middle of&nbsp;
the air as if held by an invisible hand. 
 &nbsp;

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:03.240
"Rude!" She snatched it back.
 
"Pretty good. I almost didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:08.280
see the wires," Zach smirked. 
 
"No wires, kid, just me." A cushion flipped off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:13.440
the couch on its own. The lamp tipped over on its&nbsp;
side. The tv remote careened across the room. 
 &nbsp;

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:18.840
"Yawn." Zach rolled his eyes. "We came here&nbsp;
to get scared, not for basic magic tricks."

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:24.300
"You won't be so cocky when you see&nbsp;
the next room!" Dr. Bright grimaced.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.820
"So show it to us, then." Maddie retorted.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:31.740
"I will if you just! Go that way. Yeah, that&nbsp;
door. Open it." Dr. Bright sighed. "Blah blah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.140
blah, welcome to the Infirmary.&nbsp;
Beware the patients, they bite."

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:38.640
Dr. Bright led the group&nbsp;
into a strangely bright room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:43.200
a jarring contrast to the rest of the house.&nbsp;
It was lit with buzzing fluorescent lights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.340
and contained absolutely no furniture.&nbsp;
As they walked in, they could hear the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:51.600
rattling of chains, but they couldn't make&nbsp;
out the source of the sound at first. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:56.700
a figure lurched into view: it looked like a&nbsp;
person, but there was something horribly wrong.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.980
Their skin was covered in patches of yellow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:04.140
gangrenous tissue. Their eyes were glassy and&nbsp;
vacant, and their mouth hung open in a slack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.740
empty expression. All along the&nbsp;
wall, there were people, chained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.420
up and straining steadily against their bonds,&nbsp;
shuffling toward the group as they drew closer.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:15.720
"Okay, zombies. Classic, I get it." Zach shrugged.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:19.560
"They're kind of creepy..." Maddie shivered&nbsp;
as one of the creatures snapped its jaws at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:23.940
her. It couldn't get close enough to take a&nbsp;
bite, but the intent felt real just the same.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:28.500
"They're not real. It's fine," Janie gave&nbsp;
Maddie's shoulder a comforting squeeze.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:33.660
"I'm afraid these poor souls are indeed all too&nbsp;
real." Dr. Bright's energy was restored as he saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:38.700
a bit of fear creeping into the group's sarcastic&nbsp;
demeanor. "Victims of a complex prion disease,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:43.560
one with no known cure. Once they were infected,&nbsp;
they were lost within a day. Now, they're hollow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:48.540
shells of their former selves, walking corpses&nbsp;
with only one goal: to devour the living."

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:54.540
"Sure, totally." Zach laughed, but his eyes&nbsp;
flickered nervously from zombie to zombie. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.540 --> 00:13:00.000
room smelled like decay, thick and nauseating,&nbsp;
and these people didn't seem like actors...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.920
"Next room, please!" Maddie's voice&nbsp;
shook, betraying her frazzled nerves.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:09.900
"But I haven't shown you my favorite specimen&nbsp;
yet. Over here!" Dr. Bright led the group to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:14.580
massive glass tank, where something fleshy and&nbsp;
vaguely humanoid was crouching inside. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:19.320
shaped almost like a person, but as if their&nbsp;
body had begun to melt. Skin had turned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:23.580
something soft, slick, and slimy-looking.&nbsp;
A palm slapped wetly against the glass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:28.380
and the group noticed that its fingers looked&nbsp;
webbed, excess skin growing between them and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:32.400
stretching out, making the digits look more&nbsp;
like little tentacles than something human.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:37.380
Then, it looked at them. Or rather,&nbsp;
it turned its face toward them. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:42.300
flesh had spread over the place where the eyes,&nbsp;
nostrils, and mouth should have been. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:45.240
it was just smooth and blank&nbsp;
all over. For the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.780
since they entered the haunted house,&nbsp;
the three visitors had nothing to say.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:55.320
"This is a particularly awful disease. Highly&nbsp;
contagious, highly aggressive. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.800
it's been contained...mostly.&nbsp;
Just don't tap on the glass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:01.800
you might aggravate him. Then&nbsp;
who knows what he'll do..."

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:04.260
With a creak, he opened the next door. "Shall we?"

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:07.260
The three teens nodded silently,&nbsp;
and, glancing over their shoulders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:10.740
one more time at the eerie figure in&nbsp;
the tank, quickly followed him out.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:15.840
"Enjoy the change of scenery!" Dr. Bright&nbsp;
commented, as he led the group out a side door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:19.380
back into the crisp autumn air.&nbsp;
"We're going out of the main house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:23.160
to the greenhouse over here. We could use&nbsp;
a little bit of nature, don't you think?"

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:27.300
"So, killer plants, or what?" Zach guessed.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:32.640
"You'll have to wait and see." Dr. Bright stopped&nbsp;
at the entrance to a large glass greenhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:38.880
the glass dirty and opaque from years of disuse.&nbsp;
"Prepare yourself. It's a little swampy inside."

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:43.800
In the greenhouse, naturally, there were dozens&nbsp;
of different plants: vines creeping up the walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:49.080
colorful flowers blossoming, moss hanging down&nbsp;
from the ceiling. The air was humid and hot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:53.760
a jarring change after the cool night&nbsp;
breeze just outside. The floor was flooded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:58.560
with a shallow layer of stagnant water,&nbsp;
green pond scum resting along the top.

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:01.740
"These are new shoes!" Zach groaned as his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:04.080
pristine sneakers disappeared&nbsp;
into the muck with a splash.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:06.600
"Are there bugs in here?" Maddie winced.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:10.860
"Oh, absolutely." Dr. Bright chuckled. "I&nbsp;
hope you've had all your shots, by the way."

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:15.060
"What?! What's that mean?!" Janie&nbsp;
demanded further explanation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.360
but Dr. Bright provided none. As&nbsp;
they trudged through the greenhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:22.320
the water grew deeper, climbing higher up&nbsp;
their legs until it reached their knees.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:26.220
"Ugh, what's that smell?" Janie&nbsp;
pinched her nose with a grimace.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:31.500
"Why don't you look over there and see?" Dr.&nbsp;
Bright pointed to an area just ahead, where the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:37.380
water was rippling curiously, as if something was&nbsp;
just below the surface. A dark patch of tangled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:43.440
greasy hair slowly began to surface,&nbsp;
followed by a mottled green face. Large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:47.160
wide eyes stared at the group as&nbsp;
SCP-811 emerged from the water.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:52.020
"You hungry?" Dr. Bright asked. She nodded&nbsp;
silently, looking intently at the teens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:57.000
"They're not for you, they're guests.&nbsp;
Here!" Dr. Bright produced a dead possum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.240
which he threw toward the swamp&nbsp;
woman. She held the carcass in place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:04.800
slowly melting it with the digestive fluid&nbsp;
that leaks from all of her slimy pores.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:09.540
"If I get sick from this place, my mom will&nbsp;
sue you. She's a lawyer," Janie threatened.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:13.740
"Let's move on then. We're almost at&nbsp;
the finale." Dr. Bright and the kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:17.760
left the swamp woman to digest her meal,&nbsp;
and headed back toward the main house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:22.800
"Follow me into...the basement.&nbsp;
Careful, it's dark down here."

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.740
Dr. Bright flipped a switch, and a single, dim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.940
flickering bulb illuminated the rickety&nbsp;
wooden stairs down into the blackness of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:33.600
the basement. "Watch your step. Who&nbsp;
knows how stable these stairs are?"

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:37.320
As the group descended into the depths of&nbsp;
the house, they could hear the sound of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:42.900
something sobbing, softly. Whatever it was,&nbsp;
it sounded positively heartbroken. At the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:47.640
foot of the stairs, off to the side, they&nbsp;
could see a tall, thin, pale figure with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:51.900
a burlap bag over its head. Its arms were&nbsp;
wrapped around itself, and it was shaking.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:56.640
"So what, you'll pull the bag off and it's&nbsp;
something really scary?" Maddie guessed.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:01.800
"Oh no, we won't be touching that bag. If you&nbsp;
value your life, you'll trust me when I say:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:05.340
that's not worth it. He's plenty scary&nbsp;
without getting you all eviscerated."

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:08.700
"For a creepy basement, this is&nbsp;
pretty boring," Janie sighed.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:13.620
Still, the group continued to follow Dr. Bright.&nbsp;
As they passed the Shy Guy in the burlap sack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:18.540
getting further and further away from the light&nbsp;
on the stairs, the walkway began to narrow. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:23.760
left the main room of the basement, and squeezed&nbsp;
into a tight stone pathway, one that forced them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:28.920
to walk in single file, one right behind the&nbsp;
other. They couldn't hear the sobbing anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:34.560
couldn't hear Dr. Bright making cheesy ghost&nbsp;
noises or trying to build up the atmosphere. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:39.600
they could hear were their footsteps, their hearts&nbsp;
beating, and the sound of their own breathing.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:44.340
Then, they realized...there had been&nbsp;
four sets of footsteps. But now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:49.680
they heard a fifth, coming from somewhere up&nbsp;
ahead. Whatever it was, it was getting closer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:55.440
and closer, and it sounded big. It sounded&nbsp;
like nothing they'd ever heard before. Just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:59.280
when the tension was so palpable, wound&nbsp;
so tight they couldn't take it anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:04.200
Dr. Bright clicked on a flashlight and illuminated&nbsp;
the monster that stood just before them.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:07.560
"RAAAWWRR! I AM RO-MAN!"

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.640
A massive furry creature stretched out its&nbsp;
arms, filling the chamber and leaving no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:15.780
escape. The kids screamed, louder than they&nbsp;
ever had before, and ran back the way they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.440
came. They sprinted up the stairs, back&nbsp;
through each room, and out the front door.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.080
As they sat on the grass&nbsp;
outside, catching their breath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.220
Dr. Bright emerged from the house. He was&nbsp;
beaming with pride, and he was clapping.

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:28.740
"So, I did it, didn't I? I really scared you?"

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:31.680
"Are you gonna do this again&nbsp;
next year?" Maddie asked eagerly.

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:35.220
"I wasn't impressed at first, but you&nbsp;
really pulled it off." Janie nodded.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.280
"It was pretty cool." Zach shrugged.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:42.900
"You have no idea how happy I am to hear&nbsp;
that!" Dr. Bright smiled. "Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:46.380
I'm not sure my bosses will let me&nbsp;
get away with this one again...Pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:50.640
sure I'm in big trouble for doing it this&nbsp;
time. But you three made it all worth it!"

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:53.280
"Here," Janie reached into her&nbsp;
pocket and pulled out an egg.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:56.040
"We were gonna use this later if&nbsp;
the place sucked. You earned it."

00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:01.080
Dr. Bright wiped a joyful tear from his eye,&nbsp;
accepting the gift. "Happy Halloween! Now you'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:05.160
better run along to that party before it gets&nbsp;
too late. The creatures are getting hungry."

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:09.420
As he watched the three walk away, heading&nbsp;
off to make more memories, he felt a sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:14.220
of satisfaction. No matter what the bosses&nbsp;
did to punish him, or how many containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:19.740
breaches he'd risked that day, he knew he'd given&nbsp;
those kids a Halloween they would never forget.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:26.220
Now go check out “SCP-823 - Carnival of&nbsp;
Horrors” and “SCP-097 - Old Fairgrounds”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:30.120
for more terrifying attractions from&nbsp;
the world of the SCP Foundation!

